00:41:36,990 --> 00:41:39,045
when you have a little data.

815
00:41:39,045 --> 00:41:43,190

816
00:41:43,190 --> 00:41:45,800
Yeah, so I guess one
question to ask--

817
00:41:45,800 --> 00:41:49,940
Before you move on,
in the last slide,

818
00:41:49,940 --> 00:41:53,240
what do you mean again by return
conditioning for the multitask

819
00:41:53,240 --> 00:41:55,190
part?

820
00:41:55,190 --> 00:41:57,500
Yes, if you think
about the returns-to-go

821
00:41:57,500 --> 00:42:00,290
at test time, the one
you have to feed in

822
00:42:00,290 --> 00:42:08,810
as the starting token,
as one way of specifying

823
00:42:08,810 --> 00:42:11,990
what policy you want.

824
00:42:11,990 --> 00:42:13,460
[INTERPOSING VOICES]

825
00:42:13,460 --> 00:42:15,650
How is that multi-task?

826
00:42:15,650 --> 00:42:19,160
So it is multitask
in the sense that you

827
00:42:19,160 --> 00:42:21,740
can get different policies
by changing your target

828
00:42:21,740 --> 00:42:23,030
return-to-go.

829
00:42:23,030 --> 00:42:26,510
You're essentially getting
different behaviors included.

830
00:42:26,510 --> 00:42:29,310
So think about, for instance,
the Hopper and you specify

831
00:42:29,310 --> 00:42:31,970
a return-to-go that's very low.

832
00:42:31,970 --> 00:42:36,320
So you're basically saying get
me an agent which will just

833
00:42:36,320 --> 00:42:39,530
stick around its
initial state and not

834
00:42:39,530 --> 00:42:45,930
go into uncharted territory.

835
00:42:45,930 --> 00:42:48,710
And if you give it really,
really high, then you're

836
00:42:48,710 --> 00:42:52,760
asking it to do the traditional
task, which is to hop

837
00:42:52,760 --> 00:42:55,910
and go as far as
possible without falling.

838
00:42:55,910 --> 00:42:57,650
Can you qualify
those multitasks,

839
00:42:57,650 --> 00:42:59,300
because that
basically just means

840
00:42:59,300 --> 00:43:04,590
that your return conditioning
is a cue for it to memorize,

841
00:43:04,590 --> 00:43:05,090
right?

842
00:43:05,090 --> 00:43:08,420
Which is usually one of
the pitfalls of multitask?

843
00:43:08,420 --> 00:43:11,837

844
00:43:11,837 --> 00:43:12,420
I'm not sure--

845
00:43:12,420 --> 00:43:15,090
You need a task identifier,
that's what I'm trying to say.

846
00:43:15,090 --> 00:43:18,360

847
00:43:18,360 --> 00:43:20,310
I'm not sure if
it's memorization--

848
00:43:20,310 --> 00:43:23,370

849
00:43:23,370 --> 00:43:28,410
I think the purpose
of this, I mean

850
00:43:28,410 --> 00:43:31,920
having an offline dataset
that makes it basically saying

851
00:43:31,920 --> 00:43:36,570
that it's very, very specific
to if you had the same start

852
00:43:36,570 --> 00:43:39,330
state, and you took
the same actions,

853
00:43:39,330 --> 00:43:42,240
and you had the same
target returns, that

854
00:43:42,240 --> 00:43:44,580
would qualify as memorization.

855
00:43:44,580 --> 00:43:48,420
But here at test time, we allow
all of these things to change.

856
00:43:48,420 --> 00:43:49,840
And in fact they do change.

857
00:43:49,840 --> 00:43:52,110
So your initial state
would be different.

858
00:43:52,110 --> 00:43:58,477
Your target return of it could
be a different scalar than one

859
00:43:58,477 --> 00:43:59,685
you ever saw during training.

860
00:43:59,685 --> 00:44:04,020

861
00:44:04,020 --> 00:44:07,230
So essentially, the
model has to learn

862
00:44:07,230 --> 00:44:09,090
to generate that
behavior starting

863
00:44:09,090 --> 00:44:11,820
from a different
initial state and maybe

864
00:44:11,820 --> 00:44:13,500
a different value
of the target return

865
00:44:13,500 --> 00:44:17,910
than it saw during training.

866
00:44:17,910 --> 00:44:20,850
If the dynamics are stochastic
that also makes it that.

867
00:44:20,850 --> 00:44:22,620
Even if you memorize
the actions,

868
00:44:22,620 --> 00:44:25,840
you're not guaranteed to
get the same next state.

869
00:44:25,840 --> 00:44:28,830
So you would actually
have a bad correlation

870
00:44:28,830 --> 00:44:31,610
with the performance if the
dynamics were also stochastic.

871
00:44:31,610 --> 00:44:35,660

872
00:44:35,660 --> 00:44:37,420
I also [INAUDIBLE]
how much time does it

